module Insurance.PayoutBridge where

import DA.Optional (isSome, optionalToList)
import Insurance.Types

-- Created as the on-chain consequence of a matched payout tier (see
-- Insurance.PolicyToken.PolicyToken_EvaluateTrigger). Its existence on the
-- ledger IS the "Payout_Approved" signal.
--
-- THE PLATFORM NEVER MOVES MONEY. Canton is authorization and
-- ledger-of-record only; it is never a custodian. The insurer settles the
-- indemnity through its own banking systems and then REPORTS that
-- settlement back, which is what PayoutApproved_ConfirmSettlement records.
-- This template therefore carries no IBAN, no account number and no payment
-- instruction, and none may be added -- a design rule, not an
-- oversight.
--
-- `amount` is the GROSS indemnity. Any set-off of outstanding premium
-- against it (TTK 6102 m. 1431(5) permits the insurer to deduct) is the
-- insurer's own arithmetic in its own system and is deliberately not
-- modelled here.
template PayoutApproved
  with
    insurer                : Party
    policyholder            : Party
    oracleOperator          : Party
    policyId                : Text
    coverageCode            : Text   -- which of the policy's coverages this payout came from (Stage 2 Part 2)
    -- The PolicyToken this payout was raised on. FIXED in Stage 4's
    -- termination round: it was set with `show self` inside
    -- PolicyToken_EvaluateTrigger, which on this participant renders the
    -- literal "<contract-id>" -- Canton redacts contract ids in `show` -- so
    -- from Stage 1 until now it never carried a usable reference. The
    -- caller supplies the id it is exercising against instead.
    --
    -- This link matters more since termination: the token can be archived
    -- for non-payment while payouts raised on it still exist, and this is
    -- the chain back from a payout to the policy it came from.
    sourcePolicyContractId  : Text
    amount                  : Decimal
    -- WHO this payout is owed to. One recipient per contract, never two line
    -- items on one: m. 1427 runs maturity and default per claim, so paying
    -- the bank does not discharge what is owed to the insured, and the two
    -- have to be separately settleable, failable and resolvable. The bank
    -- settles today and the insured cannot be reached -- the system must be
    -- able to say exactly that.
    --
    -- `amount` above is this recipient's own GROSS figure. The split is
    -- between recipients; nothing here is netted against anything.
    recipient               : PayoutDestinationRole
    -- Set only on a leg whose recipient IS the mortgagee, so the bank can
    -- see the payout it is owed -- a party that is neither signatory nor
    -- observer cannot fetch a contract at all, and divulgence does not
    -- rescue it. Narrower than the policy-level mortgagee, which observes
    -- the whole token including coverages its charge does not reach.
    mortgagee               : Optional Party
    currency                : Text
    payoutPercentage        : Decimal
    tierLabel                : Text
    isFullSettlement        : Bool
    -- Snapshotted from the triggering coverage at approval time (Stage 4),
    -- so the ledger can check a reported settlement against the destination
    -- the policy actually specified. Without it the role check below would
    -- have nothing on-ledger to check against.
    payoutDestination       : [PayoutDestinationRole]
    approvedAt              : Time
    -- v22. The event this payout was approved for, as the trigger
    -- received it: [eventStart, eventEnd), start inclusive, end exclusive.
    eventStart              : Time
    eventEnd                : Time
    -- v22. The digest of the evidence the trigger was evaluated on,
    -- "sha256:" + 64 lowercase hex. A digest only: no request parameters,
    -- no coordinates, reach this contract's observers.
    evidenceDigest          : Text
  where
    signatory insurer, oracleOperator
    observer policyholder, optionalToList mortgagee

    ensure amount > 0.0 && not (null payoutDestination) &&
      -- v22. With the two equal, the insurer alone could create this
      -- contract -- an equal signatory pair needs only one signature.
      oracleOperator /= insurer &&
      -- A leg can only be owed to a role the coverage actually permits --
      -- EXCEPT the enforcement office, and the exemption needs its reason
      -- stated or someone will read it as a hole.
      --
      -- payoutDestination records the destinations the policy DESIGNATED when
      -- it was written. Nobody designates an icra mudurlugu: m. 1457 routes
      -- there because the insured property was attached, which happens years
      -- after the policy is written and by someone who is not a party to it.
      -- Requiring it in the list would mean the system could only honour the
      -- article where an attachment had been anticipated at creation.
      (recipient == PDR_EnforcementOffice || recipient `elem` payoutDestination) &&
      -- A mortgagee leg with no mortgagee party would be owed to nobody
      -- reachable, and a mortgagee party on any other leg would disclose it
      -- to a party that is not its recipient.
      (recipient == PDR_Mortgagee) == isSome mortgagee

    -- Stage 4: the NORMAL path. The insurer has already paid, through its
    -- own systems, and is reporting that fact.
    --
    -- The ledger cannot verify that money moved -- nothing on-chain can.
    -- What it can do is record what the insurer ASSERTED, and refuse an
    -- assertion that contradicts the policy: paidRole must be one the
    -- coverage's own payoutDestination allows. A settlement claiming to
    -- have paid a party the policy never designated is rejected outright.
    --
    -- settledAt is the insurer's reported settlement date, supplied from
    -- outside. It is NOT a system clock reading -- same principle as the
    -- notice service date: the platform cannot observe when a bank transfer
    -- landed, only when it was told.
    --
    -- Consuming: settling closes the payout, and since v22 leaves a
    -- PayoutSettled record in its place, whose id this choice returns. Of
    -- the bank reference, the ledger holds only its salted digest,
    -- "sha256:" + hex(SHA-256(salt || text)); the raw text and the salt stay
    -- in SQL. The date and the role are on the record as
    -- reported.
    choice PayoutApproved_ConfirmSettlement : ContractId PayoutSettled
      with
        bankReference : Text
        settledAt     : Time
        paidRole      : PayoutDestinationRole
      controller insurer
      do
        assertMsg "bankReference is required to confirm a settlement"
          (bankReference /= "")
        -- Same exemption as the ensure clause above, and for the same
        -- reason: nobody designates an icra mudurlugu when the policy is
        -- written, so m. 1457's recipient is never in this list. The
        -- recipient check below is the operative one for such a leg.
        assertMsg ("settlement reports paying " <> show paidRole <>
                   ", which is not among this coverage's payoutDestination")
          (paidRole == PDR_EnforcementOffice || paidRole `elem` payoutDestination)
        -- Each contract is owed to ONE recipient since v17, so a settlement
        -- report naming a different one is not merely unusual -- it says the
        -- insurer paid someone other than the party this obligation is to,
        -- and would close the wrong claim.
        assertMsg ("settlement reports paying " <> show paidRole <>
                   ", but this payout is owed to " <> show recipient)
          (paidRole == recipient)
        recordedAt <- getTime
        create PayoutSettled with
          insurer
          policyholder
          mortgagee
          oracleOperator
          policyId
          coverageCode
          sourcePayoutContractId = Some self
          amount
          currency
          recipient = paidRole
          eventStart
          eventEnd
          evidenceDigest
          settledAt
          bankReferenceDigest = bankReference
          recordedAt

    -- Stage 4: the EXCEPTION path, and only that. Until Stage 4 every
    -- payout came through here, because no settlement path existed and the
    -- dispatcher called this unconditionally. That is no longer the
    -- default: nothing routes a payout here automatically any more, and it
    -- fires only when the insurer reports a genuine failure -- a closed
    -- account, a payee that cannot be found, a dispute.
    choice PayoutApproved_MarkFailed : ContractId ManualReviewRequired
      with
        failureReason : Text
        -- The link back to the payout this review item came from, passed in
        -- rather than derived. `show self` CANNOT be used: on this
        -- participant it renders the literal string "<contract-id>", not an
        -- id -- Canton redacts contract ids in `show`. Found in Stage 4's
        -- live verification, and the reason the pre-existing
        -- sourcePolicyContractId field on this template had been recording a
        -- placeholder since Stage 1. That one was fixed the same way in v12
        -- (PolicyToken_EvaluateTrigger now takes selfContractId); this
        -- comment is kept because the trap it describes is a property of the
        -- participant, not of either field.
        --
        -- The caller (dispatch/dispatcher.js) already holds the exact
        -- contract id it is exercising against, so it supplies it.
        sourcePayoutContractId : Text
      controller insurer
      do
        assertMsg "failureReason is required to mark a payout failed"
          (failureReason /= "")
        assertMsg "sourcePayoutContractId is required -- it is the link back to the payout"
          (sourcePayoutContractId /= "")
        -- v22. flaggedAt is the transaction's ledger time, not a value
        -- the caller supplies.
        now <- getTime
        create ManualReviewRequired with
          insurer
          policyholder
          policyId
          coverageCode
          -- Before Stage 4 only policyId travelled, which is ambiguous the
          -- moment a policy has more than one payout -- the chain back to
          -- the specific PayoutApproved was simply lost.
          sourcePayoutContractId
          amount
          currency
          reason = failureReason
          flaggedAt = now
          oracleOperator
          mortgagee
          recipient = Some recipient
          sourcePayoutCid = Some self
          eventStart
          eventEnd
          evidenceDigest

-- Landing spot when a payout could not be settled through the normal path.
-- Until Stage 4 this had no choices at all beyond the implicit Archive, so
-- a review item that was created could never be closed with a recorded
-- outcome -- the queue only grew. It now has exactly two exits, and both
-- record what happened. There is deliberately no third exit that discards
-- an item without an outcome.
template ManualReviewRequired
  with
    insurer                : Party
    policyholder           : Party
    policyId               : Text
    coverageCode           : Text   -- carried through the whole chain (Stage 4)
    sourcePayoutContractId : Text   -- contract id of the PayoutApproved this came from, supplied by the caller
    amount                 : Decimal
    currency               : Text
    reason                 : Text
    flaggedAt              : Time
    -- v22. What a closing record needs and this item cannot otherwise
    -- reach, because the PayoutApproved it came from is archived. Carried
    -- from that payout by MarkFailed; on an item the trigger raised for an
    -- unrouted amount there is no source payout, so the payout-only fields
    -- are None. None of them is an observer here: `mortgagee` becomes one
    -- on the closing record only, as it was on the payout.
    -- v22. Except `mortgagee`: on an unrouted item raised on a charged
    -- coverage it is the policy's charge holder, carried so the item can be
    -- settled to it; it reaches a record only as that record's recipient.
    oracleOperator         : Party
    mortgagee              : Optional Party
    recipient              : Optional PayoutDestinationRole
    sourcePayoutCid        : Optional (ContractId PayoutApproved)
    eventStart             : Time
    eventEnd               : Time
    evidenceDigest         : Text
  where
    signatory insurer
    observer policyholder

    -- Exit 1: it was settled after all, outside the normal flow. Same
    -- evidence as PayoutApproved_ConfirmSettlement, different starting
    -- contract -- deliberately identical arguments so the two paths produce
    -- the same record.
    --
    -- The role check cannot be made here: payoutDestination lives on
    -- PayoutApproved, which this item's creation archived. The reported
    -- role is recorded as asserted, and the check is enforced off-ledger by
    -- dispatch/dispatcher.js against the coverage's SQL mirror instead.
    choice ManualReviewRequired_ResolveSettled : ContractId PayoutSettled
      with
        bankReference : Text
        settledAt     : Time
        paidRole      : PayoutDestinationRole
      controller insurer
      do
        assertMsg "bankReference is required to resolve a review item as settled"
          (bankReference /= "")
        -- v22. An item MarkFailed raised carries its payout's recipient,
        -- and a report naming another role would close the wrong claim, as
        -- in ConfirmSettlement. An unrouted item carries none and its role is
        -- not checked here. v22: one raised on a charged coverage carries
        -- the mortgagee party, so PDR_Mortgagee is accepted for it; with no
        -- mortgagee party the record's own ensure still refuses it.
        assertMsg ("settlement reports paying " <> show paidRole <>
                   ", but this item is owed to " <> show recipient)
          (optional True (== paidRole) recipient)
        -- v22: the same record ConfirmSettlement leaves.
        recordedAt <- getTime
        create PayoutSettled with
          insurer
          policyholder
          -- v22. Only on a record paid to the mortgagee, so an unrouted
          -- item's charge holder observes nothing it was not paid.
          mortgagee = if paidRole == PDR_Mortgagee then mortgagee else None
          oracleOperator
          policyId
          coverageCode
          sourcePayoutContractId = sourcePayoutCid
          amount
          currency
          recipient = paidRole
          eventStart
          eventEnd
          evidenceDigest
          settledAt
          bankReferenceDigest = bankReference
          recordedAt

    -- Exit 2: it will not be paid, and that is the final answer. An
    -- enumerated reason so the outcome is queryable, plus a mandatory
    -- free-text note so the specific circumstances are not flattened into
    -- the enum.
    --
    -- Recording an outcome is not a legal conclusion about whether the
    -- indemnity was lawfully extinguished. It records what the insurer
    -- asserted and why.
    choice ManualReviewRequired_ResolveUnpaid : ContractId PayoutClosedUnpaid
      with
        unpaidReason : UnpaidReason
        note         : Text
        -- v22. The instant the insurer declares the item closed,
        -- supplied like settledAt; the record's own ledger time is separate.
        closedAt     : Time
      controller insurer
      do
        assertMsg "a note is required when closing a review item unpaid"
          (note /= "")
        recordedAt <- getTime
        create PayoutClosedUnpaid with
          insurer
          policyholder
          -- v22. As in ResolveSettled: an unrouted item's charge holder
          -- is not carried onto a record it would then observe.
          mortgagee = if recipient == Some PDR_Mortgagee then mortgagee else None
          oracleOperator
          policyId
          coverageCode
          sourcePayoutContractId = sourcePayoutCid
          amount
          currency
          recipient
          eventStart
          eventEnd
          evidenceDigest
          unpaidReason
          noteDigest = note
          closedAt
          recordedAt

-- v22. What stays on the ledger once a payout is reported settled,
-- through PayoutApproved_ConfirmSettlement or
-- ManualReviewRequired_ResolveSettled. It is the insurer's DECLARATION that
-- it paid, not proof that money moved: the platform never moves money and
-- cannot observe a bank transfer (see PayoutApproved above).
--
-- No choice other than the implicit Archive. The platform never archives
-- one; the signatory can, since Daml lets a signatory archive any contract
-- it signs, so "never goes" cannot be enforced here.
--
-- Observers are the source payout's: the policyholder, and the mortgagee
-- only on a leg that was the mortgagee's own. oracleOperator is a plain
-- field, neither signatory nor observer.
template PayoutSettled
  with
    insurer                : Party
    policyholder           : Party
    mortgagee              : Optional Party
    oracleOperator         : Party
    policyId               : Text
    coverageCode           : Text
    -- The PayoutApproved this settles. None when the review item it came
    -- from was raised by the trigger for an unrouted amount and so had no
    -- source payout.
    sourcePayoutContractId : Optional (ContractId PayoutApproved)
    amount                 : Decimal
    currency               : Text
    -- The role the insurer reports having paid.
    recipient              : PayoutDestinationRole
    eventStart             : Time
    eventEnd               : Time
    evidenceDigest         : Text
    -- The insurer's reported settlement date.
    settledAt              : Time
    -- "sha256:" + hex(SHA-256(salt || bank reference)); the text and the
    -- salt stay in SQL.
    bankReferenceDigest    : Text
    -- The ledger time of the transaction that created this record.
    recordedAt             : Time
  where
    signatory insurer
    observer policyholder, optionalToList mortgagee

    ensure oracleOperator /= insurer && isSha256Digest bankReferenceDigest &&
      -- v22. PayoutApproved's rule, for the same reason.
      (recipient == PDR_Mortgagee) == isSome mortgagee

-- v22. What stays on the ledger once a review item is closed unpaid,
-- through ManualReviewRequired_ResolveUnpaid. The insurer's declaration and
-- why, as there; not a legal conclusion that the indemnity was lawfully
-- extinguished. Same rules as PayoutSettled: no choice but Archive, the
-- platform never archives it, same observers, oracleOperator a plain field.
template PayoutClosedUnpaid
  with
    insurer                : Party
    policyholder           : Party
    mortgagee              : Optional Party
    oracleOperator         : Party
    policyId               : Text
    coverageCode           : Text
    sourcePayoutContractId : Optional (ContractId PayoutApproved)
    amount                 : Decimal
    currency               : Text
    -- The source payout's recipient; None on an unrouted amount, which was
    -- never owed to a role.
    recipient              : Optional PayoutDestinationRole
    eventStart             : Time
    eventEnd               : Time
    evidenceDigest         : Text
    unpaidReason           : UnpaidReason
    -- "sha256:" + hex(SHA-256(salt || note)); the note and the salt stay in
    -- SQL.
    noteDigest             : Text
    -- The insurer's declared closing instant.
    closedAt               : Time
    -- The ledger time of the transaction that created this record.
    recordedAt             : Time
  where
    signatory insurer
    observer policyholder, optionalToList mortgagee

    ensure oracleOperator /= insurer && isSha256Digest noteDigest &&
      -- v22. PayoutApproved's rule; an unrouted amount has no recipient
      -- and so no mortgagee.
      (recipient == Some PDR_Mortgagee) == isSome mortgagee
